# WolkaraForever layer patch 0900 - Local signing: capture the final code pages
#
# Why: WoW clients unpack their own code at launch, so their Local signing page
# container must be built from a capture of the final __TEXT pages
# (tools/build_signed_container.py --capture, TOLKARA_CAPTURE), and the platform
# documents that the app cannot produce one yet. Local signing skips the
# Developer service arena preparation, which takes ~37 s per launch on an iPhone.
#
# With --capture-final-pages on a Developer service launch, the runtime writes
# the guest's __TEXT, as it is once the first (unpacking) initializer returned,
# to Documents/LocalSigning/capture.bin (mode 0600, written then renamed). That
# is the same point and the same bytes Local signing's own startup check
# compares against the container. Off by default; never under Local signing;
# only the byte count is logged. The capture is the user's own derived copy and
# stays on their device and in ignored build output, never in the repository.
#
# Applies to: runtime/SignedImage.c, runtime/SignedImage.h,
#             runtime/NativeGuest.m, tests/test_signed_image.c
# Upstream: no - personal feature, carried on raven/integration only.
#
